[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Persistence [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mHow should the identity persist?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mCookie + localStorage label (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mServer sets an HttpOnly session cookie (the real credential); userId lives in localStorage as a non-secret label [39m
     [38;5;246mthe server re-verifies. XSS can read the label but not steal the session.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m localStorage only
     [38;5;246mSimplest code, survives restarts. Persists on shared machines and is readable by any XSS — acceptable only if [39m
     [38;5;246mnothing ever trusts it.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m sessionStorage only
     [38;5;246mTab-scoped, auto-cleared, narrower exposure. Loses "stay logged in" — every new tab starts logged out.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
